1
00:00:08,016 --> 00:00:11,822
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:13,002 --> 00:00:25,528
This Queen was, what we call today; very democratic or shuraa(شوری) a better word; She would seek the advice of her followers.

3
00:00:25,995 --> 00:00:32,148
And Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! We see in this Queen many good qualities before Islam.

4
00:00:33,261 --> 00:00:35,834
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى guided her through her Hikmah(حكمة).

5
00:00:37,401 --> 00:00:44,585
You can see from her personality; that she was very wise and her wisdom ended up leading her into Islam.

6
00:00:45,285 --> 00:00:56,294
Because Al-Aqal(العقل); the mind would lead us toward truth, would lead us to understand the message of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); by the will of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

7
00:00:56,974 --> 00:01:02,780
And that's why; the non-believers on the day of judgment, no matter how intelligent they were on the face of the earth,

8
00:01:02,907 --> 00:01:07,293
on the day of judgment when they see the punishment and they see hellfire; what would they say?

9
00:01:07,813 --> 00:01:12,452
وَقَالُواْ لَوْ كُنَّا نَسْمَعُ أَوْ نَعْقِلُ مَا كُنَّا فِىٓ أَصْحَٰبِ الْجَحِيم۝

10
00:01:13,466 --> 00:01:22,231
They would say; If we used to hear, or if we had understanding; we wouldn't have been in hellfire.

11
00:01:23,725 --> 00:01:27,877
So they say; we didn't have any understanding when we're on earth, and we didn't have any hearing.

12
00:01:28,584 --> 00:01:35,096
So the true mind and the true understanding; is the understanding that would lead a person towards the truth or lead the person towards Islam.

13
00:01:35,716 --> 00:01:39,042
She was soliciting advice from her Mala'(مَلَاْ);

14
00:01:39,115 --> 00:01:45,143
Al-Mala'(اَلْمَلَاْ) in Qur'an means; the chiefs or the leaders of the society, Al-Mala'(اَلْمَلَاْ).

15
00:01:45,663 --> 00:01:52,419
قَالَتْ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلْمَلَؤُاْ أَفْتُونِى فِىٓ أَمْرِى

16
00:01:52,805 --> 00:01:57,323
She said; Oh chiefs! Advise me in this case of mine.

17
00:01:58,223 --> 00:01:59,190
And then she said;

18
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:06,162
مَا كُنتُ قَاطِعَةً أَمْرًا حَتَّىٰ تَشْهَدُونِ۝

19
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:10,758
I decide no case to you are present with me and give me your opinions.

20
00:02:11,264 --> 00:02:13,183
She said; I want your advice on this case.

21
00:02:13,370 --> 00:02:18,950
And then she said; and you know me, I never take a decision until I seek your advice; Shuraa(شوری).

22
00:02:19,782 --> 00:02:21,159
Their response was;

23
00:02:21,399 --> 00:02:29,007
قَالُواْ نَحْنُ أُوْلُواْ قُوَّةٍۢ وَأُوْلُواْ بَأْسٍۢ شَدِيدٍۢ

24
00:02:29,354 --> 00:02:34,090
They said; We have great strength and great ability for war.

25
00:02:35,023 --> 00:02:40,883
They said, if you want us to fight, we're ready; The army is prepared; It's powerful; We're ready to go to war.

26
00:02:41,276 --> 00:02:42,189
And then they said;

27
00:02:42,369 --> 00:02:48,808
وَٱلْأَمْرُ إِلَيْكِ فَٱنظُرِى مَاذَا تَأْمُرِينَ۝

28
00:02:49,368 --> 00:02:54,061
But it is for you to command, so think over what you will command.

29
00:02:54,954 --> 00:02:58,371
So their opinion was; we are ready to do whatever you want us to do.

30
00:02:58,411 --> 00:02:59,971
If you want us to fight; we're ready to fight.

31
00:03:00,984 --> 00:03:03,196
So they gave her the green light to go to war.

32
00:03:04,449 --> 00:03:08,996
Actually, maybe they encouraged her; they said; we are ready to fight, it's your decision now.

33
00:03:09,962 --> 00:03:12,445
Her wisdom now shows up.

34
00:03:13,338 --> 00:03:17,065
She wants to deal with the situation in the softest way possible.

35
00:03:17,625 --> 00:03:22,726
And confrontation could be an option, but later.

36
00:03:23,533 --> 00:03:27,443
Why start with confrontation when there are other means?

37
00:03:28,050 --> 00:03:32,522
And we know that, that was the policy of Rasool Allah ﷺ in dealing with situations.

38
00:03:33,969 --> 00:03:36,069
Rasool Allah ﷺ was described as;

39
00:03:36,369 --> 00:03:39,440
ما خيربين أمرين إلا أختار أيسرهما

40
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:45,677
Whenever Rasool Allah ﷺ would be offered two options, he would always choose the easiest.

41
00:03:45,897 --> 00:03:54,710
Rasool Allah ﷺ would try to avoid confrontation, whether it is with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) or any other people as much as he can.

42
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:57,690
And this was the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

43
00:03:58,690 --> 00:04:03,182
And that's why, when in Sulh al-Hudaybiyah(صلح الحديبية); an agreement was reached.

44
00:04:03,422 --> 00:04:08,578
Rasool Allah ﷺ accepted it even though, many of Sahabahرضى الله عنهم were reluctant to accept it.

45
00:04:08,932 --> 00:04:11,858
Because they felt that we're ready to fight.

46
00:04:12,598 --> 00:04:16,944
But we should not understand that this means, we give our principles

47
00:04:17,178 --> 00:04:22,571
or we compromise in the religion, as we find in the peace process that's happening now.

48
00:04:22,917 --> 00:04:23,977
That's something different.

49
00:04:24,364 --> 00:04:30,409
That is not peace; It is giving up; all of your principles and giving up; the Muslim land.

50
00:04:30,676 --> 00:04:31,969
That's not called peace.

51
00:04:32,236 --> 00:04:34,325
It's misleading; the naming itself is misleading.

52
00:04:36,518 --> 00:04:39,524
What was the response of Al-Malikah(الملكه); the queen?

53
00:04:39,824 --> 00:04:40,577
She said;

54
00:04:40,810 --> 00:04:56,072
قَالَتْ إِنَّ ٱلْمُلُوكَ إِذَا دَخَلُواْ قَرْيَةً أَفْسَدُوهَا وَجَعَلُوٓاْ أَعِزَّةَ أَهْلِهَآ أَذِلَّةً ۖ وَكَذَٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُونَ۝

55
00:04:56,739 --> 00:05:06,722
She said; Verily kings; when they enter a town, they despoil it and make the most honorable amongst its people; the lowest.

56
00:05:07,242 --> 00:05:09,571
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى approved what she said and said;

57
00:05:09,597 --> 00:05:10,364
And thus they do;

58
00:05:10,404 --> 00:05:11,257
وَكَذَٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُونَ۝

59
00:05:12,357 --> 00:05:13,678
What did she mean by this?

60
00:05:14,211 --> 00:05:17,031
When the Kings enter into our land, they corrupt it.

61
00:05:17,784 --> 00:05:26,630
She means that, when you enter into a confrontation with another nation; king or president or government whatever,

62
00:05:26,650 --> 00:05:31,345
when you enter into confrontation with another state or nation,

63
00:05:32,342 --> 00:05:40,100
and the other nation wins through war; when they entered into the land, they would occupy it.

64
00:05:41,126 --> 00:05:45,086
And they would disrupt the system that was there because; they entered by force.

65
00:05:46,719 --> 00:05:50,538
And because they were fighting another government.

66
00:05:50,745 --> 00:05:53,545
Because who's the one who took the decision to fight; is the government.

67
00:05:54,132 --> 00:06:00,478
They would make that government and the king or whoever is in position of responsibility; the lowest.

68
00:06:01,331 --> 00:06:07,880
Because they are our enemy; I won against you; you were the one was fighting me; you're going to be the lowest, most likely they killed them.

69
00:06:09,607 --> 00:06:12,023
But then they need assistance from the local people.

70
00:06:12,043 --> 00:06:13,369
So who do they promote?

71
00:06:14,063 --> 00:06:21,285
They usually promote the lowest class, who are enemies of the former government.

72
00:06:22,345 --> 00:06:27,173
And that's something that you find always in wars between states.

73
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:36,123
So the Queen over here is saying; If we enter into a war with Sulaimanعليه السلام and he wins through war,

74
00:06:36,616 --> 00:06:40,762
then us; the government, we're going to be done with, he's going to get rid of us.

75
00:06:41,449 --> 00:06:46,222
And he's going to take our land as; Ghaneemah(غنيمه), he's going to invade our land and occupy it.

76
00:06:46,595 --> 00:06:51,833
And he will do corruption to our land, because she is assuming that Sulaiman(سليمان) is like any other King.

77
00:06:52,273 --> 00:06:57,460
She doesn't know that Sulaiman(سليمان) is different, he's a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

78
00:06:58,260 --> 00:07:03,781
And we find; how corrupt the Muslim lands were under the European occupation.

79
00:07:04,074 --> 00:07:07,673
And now we are still suffering from that corruption until this moment.

80
00:07:08,460 --> 00:07:10,813
Because they entered through a state of war.

81
00:07:11,293 --> 00:07:17,405
So she said; I will send them a gift, rather than fighting them.

82
00:07:17,732 --> 00:07:27,797
وَإِنِّى مُرْسِلَةٌ إِلَيْهِم بِهَدِيَّةٍۢ فَنَاظِرَةٌۢ بِمَ يَرْجِعُ ٱلْمُرْسَلُونَ۝

83
00:07:28,251 --> 00:07:33,803
But verily, I'm going to send him a present, and see with what answer the messengers return.

84
00:07:34,383 --> 00:07:38,303
This method of dealing really shows her intelligence.

85
00:07:38,363 --> 00:07:42,352
Because; it's going to work, if Sulaimanعليه السلام was not a prophet.

86
00:07:43,499 --> 00:07:45,765
Because, why do kings invade lands?

87
00:07:46,605 --> 00:07:49,564
Why do governments go in war to other countries?

88
00:07:50,204 --> 00:07:51,004
Money;

89
00:07:52,031 --> 00:07:55,184
to take that land as a Ghaneemah(غنيمه).

90
00:07:57,084 --> 00:08:01,064
So she wants to send a gift, to Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان),

91
00:08:02,091 --> 00:08:07,741
to convince him that, we're going to pay you rather than go to war with us and spend a lot of money in war;

92
00:08:08,041 --> 00:08:12,140
we're going to give you whatever you want here, I'll send you a gift and see what your response will be.

93
00:08:13,193 --> 00:08:14,253
She called it a gift.

94
00:08:14,567 --> 00:08:21,676
We can maybe call it a gift, but it seems that's it's little bit tilting towards being a bride.

95
00:08:22,689 --> 00:08:24,298
And as she said; I will see what happens.

96
00:08:24,691 --> 00:08:26,531
فَنَاظِرَةٌۢ بِمَ يَرْجِعُ ٱلْمُرْسَلُونَ۝

97
00:08:26,558 --> 00:08:31,487
I'm going to see, what the response is.

98
00:08:33,807 --> 00:08:35,773
فَلَمَّا جَآءَ سُلَيْمَٰنَ

99
00:08:36,667 --> 00:08:40,029
So when the messengers with the present came to Sulaiman(سليمان);

100
00:08:40,575 --> 00:08:42,669
قَالَ أَتُمِدُّونَنِ بِمَالٍۢ

101
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:46,711
Sulaimanعليه السلام said; Will you help me in wealth?

102
00:08:47,244 --> 00:08:50,950
فَمَآ ءَاتَىٰنِۦَ ٱللَّهُ خَيْرٌ مِّمَّآ ءَاتَىٰكُم

103
00:08:51,363 --> 00:08:55,003
What Allah has given me, is better than what He has given to you.

104
00:08:55,795 --> 00:08:59,235
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said; Are you trying to give me money?

105
00:08:59,528 --> 00:09:02,624
He said; first of all what Allah has given me is better than what you have.

106
00:09:03,037 --> 00:09:04,157
What can you offer me?

107
00:09:04,570 --> 00:09:10,013
And many of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) say that, Sulaimanعليه السلام here was not referring to the material possessions that he has.

108
00:09:10,213 --> 00:09:13,933
Even though, his material possessions are better than theirs.

109
00:09:14,166 --> 00:09:21,743
But Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام was referring to the Nabuwwah(نبوّة) that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given him; the prophet-hood and the Ilm(علم) of religion.

110
00:09:22,383 --> 00:09:25,277
What I have is better than, what you have. And then he said;

111
00:09:25,757 --> 00:09:27,437
بَلْ أَنتُم بِهَدِيَّتِكُمْ تَفْرَحُونَ۝

112
00:09:27,457 --> 00:09:29,391
You are the ones who are happy with gifts.

113
00:09:30,624 --> 00:09:32,485
You cannot buy me with this gift.

114
00:09:32,952 --> 00:09:36,112
This gift is not what will make me happy and pleasant.

115
00:09:36,418 --> 00:09:39,234
You are the ones who can be bought off by gifts.

116
00:09:39,754 --> 00:09:43,488
Gifts make you happy, but this strategy will not work with me.

117
00:09:43,848 --> 00:09:46,000
And then Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام said;

118
00:09:46,147 --> 00:09:54,062
ٱرْجِعْ إِلَيْهِمْ فَلَنَأْتِيَنَّهُم بِجُنُودٍۢ لَّا قِبَلَ لَهُم بِهَا وَلَنُخْرِجَنَّهُم مِّنْهَآ أَذِلَّةً وَهُمْ صَٰغِرُونَ۝

119
00:09:54,476 --> 00:09:55,314
He said;

120
00:09:56,480 --> 00:10:01,037
Then Solomon; Sulaiman(سليمان) said to the Chief of her messengers, who brought the present;

121
00:10:01,137 --> 00:10:07,513
Go back to them, we verily shall come to them, with hosts that they cannot resist,

122
00:10:07,947 --> 00:10:13,879
and we shall drive them out of their land in disgrace, and they will be abased.

123
00:10:14,525 --> 00:10:22,364
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said; Go back and tell her, that we are going to send her an army that she will not be able to resist,

124
00:10:22,818 --> 00:10:26,464
and we are going to drive them out of their land in a state of humility.

125
00:10:28,057 --> 00:10:32,196
Sulaimanعليه السلام said; Don't give me these gifts; take your gifts back and we refused the gifts.

126
00:10:33,942 --> 00:10:36,498
So the messengers went back to her and told her; he refused the gifts.

127
00:10:36,592 --> 00:10:41,110
She realized; this was the first step in her realizing that, this man is not a man of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

128
00:10:41,883 --> 00:10:46,215
He's not a man of this world; he's not seeking Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); he's up to something else.

129
00:10:47,661 --> 00:10:50,848
And that was the first step for her to come towards the religion.

130
00:10:52,448 --> 00:10:54,953
She decided not to go to war.

131
00:10:55,146 --> 00:10:58,859
Even though, Sulaimanعليه السلام gave her a clear threat.

132
00:10:59,913 --> 00:11:03,194
She decided; she's not going to go to war, and she's going to go and meet him personally.

133
00:11:04,101 --> 00:11:09,689
She prepared her delegation, and they went out to meet with Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

134
00:11:11,042 --> 00:11:15,756
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) when she was on her way, said to his chiefs;

135
00:11:16,582 --> 00:11:27,085
قَالَ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلْمَلَؤُاْ أَيُّكُمْ يَأْتِينِى بِعَرْشِهَا قَبْلَ أَن يَأْتُونِى مُسْلِمِينَ۝

136
00:11:27,831 --> 00:11:35,130
He said; Oh chiefs! Which of you can bring me her throne, before they come to me surrendering themselves in obedience?

137
00:11:35,730 --> 00:11:41,173
What did the Hudhud(هدهد) describes; what did the bird describe in the kingdom of Saba'(سَبَإٍ)?

138
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:43,420
He describe the throne.

139
00:11:44,006 --> 00:11:46,082
The throne was the symbol of their kingdom.

140
00:11:46,749 --> 00:11:49,262
The throne was their pride.

141
00:11:50,029 --> 00:11:56,485
This was a unique thing that only the kingdom of Saba'(سَبَإٍ) had; it was the symbol of their kingdom.

142
00:11:57,071 --> 00:12:01,066
Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said; Bring it to me, before they come to me.

143
00:12:02,866 --> 00:12:08,216
Now you might ask the question; how come Sulaimanعليه السلام wanted to bring the throne; What's the reason?

144
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:13,498
Well, the scholars; the Mufassireen(مفسرين) have responded to that; They said;

145
00:12:15,058 --> 00:12:20,373
that Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام wanted to show her miracle.

146
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:29,824
The Ambiyaaعليهم السلام; they exhibit their miracles in front of the people to prove the authenticity of the message.

147
00:12:30,598 --> 00:12:36,201
They do that; one of the methods they do that; is through the miracles; presenting the miracles to the society.

148
00:12:37,155 --> 00:12:42,435
And we know that something unique about Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام was his kingdom.

149
00:12:43,241 --> 00:12:45,024
هَبْ لِى مُلْكًا لَّا يَنۢبَغِى لِأَحَدٍۢ مِّنۢ بَعْدِىٓ ۖ

150
00:12:45,044 --> 00:12:47,313
Oh Allah! Give me a kingdom, that will occur to nobody after me.

151
00:12:47,339 --> 00:12:50,773
So the kingdom of Sulaiman(سليمان) was his miracle.

152
00:12:52,073 --> 00:13:00,288
And he wanted to present to her; some of the powers that are under his control by the will of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

153
00:13:00,701 --> 00:13:04,274
to show her that, he's a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

154
00:13:04,967 --> 00:13:06,667
And he's not just a king.

155
00:13:07,187 --> 00:13:11,466
Because, this was something out of the capability of kings in that time.

156
00:13:12,959 --> 00:13:16,427
So he wanted to bring the throne before she arrives.

157
00:13:16,973 --> 00:13:20,997
The first offer was made by; Ifreet min-al-Jinn(عِفْرِيتٌ مِّنَ ٱلْجِنِّ).

158
00:13:22,093 --> 00:13:32,262
Ifreet(عِفْرِيت) is a name given to somebody who has excelled in his field and reached to the highest levels; it's called Ifreet(عِفْرِيت).

159
00:13:33,089 --> 00:13:40,268
So, Ifreet min-al-Jinn( عِفْرِيتٌ مِّنَ ٱلْجِنِّ); Ifreet(عِفْرِيت) of the Jinn(جِن) who is at the highest levels of power among the Jinn(جِن).

160
00:13:41,088 --> 00:13:42,555
You call that Jinn(جِن); Ifreet(عِفْرِيت).

161
00:13:42,902 --> 00:13:48,001
So, he's not just a Jinn(جِن), but he's Ifreet(عِفْرِيت) from the Jinn(جِن); powerful Jinn(جِن).

162
00:13:48,621 --> 00:13:53,838
And the word nowadays, in Arabic has been always used in reference to Jinn(جِن),

163
00:13:53,878 --> 00:14:01,040
but in the Arabic language, it could mean; somebody who has excelled and reached very high level in that particular field.

164
00:14:02,213 --> 00:14:04,713
Ifreet min-al-Jinn(عِفْرِيتٌ مِّنَ ٱلْجِنِّ); he made an offer. He said;

165
00:14:05,166 --> 00:14:15,235
قَالَ عِفْرِيتٌ مِّنَ ٱلْجِنِّ أَنَا۠ ءَاتِيكَ بِهِۦ قَبْلَ أَن تَقُومَ مِن مَّقَامِكَ ۖ

166
00:14:15,609 --> 00:14:21,541
وَإِنِّى عَلَيْهِ لَقَوِىٌّ أَمِينٌ۝

167
00:14:22,005 --> 00:14:28,480
Ifreet(عِفْرِيت), a strong one from the Jinn(جِن) said; I will bring it to you before you rise from your place,

168
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:32,651
and verily I am indeed strong and trustworthy for such work.

169
00:14:33,018 --> 00:14:41,492
His credentials; his resume was that I'm strong and trustworthy, and I can bring it to you before you rise up from your council.

170
00:14:41,732 --> 00:14:48,726
It is said that, Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام used to sit in Majlis al-Qadha(مجلس القضا); his government seat; his throne.

171
00:14:49,146 --> 00:14:51,166
He used to sit in it from Fajr(فجر) until Dhuhr(ظهر).

172
00:14:52,553 --> 00:14:54,747
So depend it on, when this offer was made.

173
00:14:54,987 --> 00:14:57,387
We can know that it's a few hours.

174
00:14:59,101 --> 00:15:09,496
And from Yemen to Jerusalem is maybe four hours flight by airplane; four or five hours; That's how long it would take by air.

175
00:15:10,276 --> 00:15:12,463
So this Ifreet(عِفْرِيت) was around that speed.

176
00:15:12,823 --> 00:15:17,918
Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ) exactly; how long it was; but they say that, he used to sit between Fajr(فجر) until Dhuhr(ظهر).

177
00:15:18,251 --> 00:15:20,713
Even though, according to the standards of that time;

178
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:30,878
this was something that was out of the reach of anyone, to bring it in a few hours when the methods of transportation in their time was horse and camel.

179
00:15:32,312 --> 00:15:36,558
Nevertheless, there was a better offer and Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام turned this offer down.

180
00:15:36,718 --> 00:15:38,131
A few hours was not enough.

181
00:15:38,638 --> 00:15:40,950
Because he got another offer from;

182
00:15:41,217 --> 00:15:43,557
الَّذِي عِندَهُ عِلْمٌ مِّنَ الْكِتَابِ

183
00:15:44,043 --> 00:15:46,315
The one who has knowledge of the book.

184
00:15:47,102 --> 00:15:48,969
And this shows you the power of knowledge.

185
00:15:50,009 --> 00:15:54,848
The one who has knowledge, had a better offer than the Ifreet(عِفْرِيت) of the Jinn(جِن).

186
00:15:55,395 --> 00:15:56,708
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

187
00:15:57,001 --> 00:16:08,024
قَالَ الَّذِي عِندَهُ عِلْمٌ مِّنَ الْكِتَابِ أَنَا آتِيكَ بِهِ قَبْلَ أَن يَرْتتَدَّ إِلَيْكَ طَرْفُكَ ۚ

188
00:16:09,204 --> 00:16:13,245
One with whom, who has knowledge of the Scriptures said;

189
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:17,899
I will bring it to you within the twinkling of an eye.

190
00:16:18,699 --> 00:16:22,561
Before your eye blinks; the throne is going to be in front of you.

191
00:16:24,687 --> 00:16:26,273
Ilm(علم); we know that, it's knowledge.

192
00:16:26,407 --> 00:16:27,420
What type of knowledge?

193
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,033
We don't know.

194
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:30,367
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; Al-Kitab(الكتاب); the Scripture.

195
00:16:31,273 --> 00:16:32,093
What scripture?

196
00:16:32,373 --> 00:16:36,700
Was it a scripture of Dawood(داؤد); Whether it was a different scripture; What exactly?

197
00:16:36,893 --> 00:16:44,493
We do not involve in this discussion, because this is Ghayb(غيب); it is unknown.

198
00:16:44,860 --> 00:16:50,149
What we know is; what Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told us in Qur'an, and we do not follow the Israiliyat(اسرائيليات) stories.

199
00:16:50,389 --> 00:16:57,814
We don't go after that, but we stop at what information, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has provided us with.

200
00:16:58,081 --> 00:17:00,481
We know that it's knowledge and we learned from this;

201
00:17:00,774 --> 00:17:02,402
That knowledge, has power.

202
00:17:04,149 --> 00:17:08,869
With the twinkling of an eye; the throne was right there in front of Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

203
00:17:10,516 --> 00:17:13,056
This is power under the hands of Sulaiman(سليمان).

204
00:17:14,189 --> 00:17:16,354
What was the response of Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام?

205
00:17:17,154 --> 00:17:30,102
فَلَمَّا رَآهُ مُسْتَقِرًّا عِندَهُ قَالَ هَٰذَا مِن فَضْلِ رَبِّي لِيَبْلُوَنِي أَأَشْكُرُ أَمْ أَكْفُرُ ۖ

206
00:17:31,022 --> 00:17:36,618
When he saw it placed before him, he said; This is by the grace of my Lord.

207
00:17:37,578 --> 00:17:41,485
He didn't say; this is by the grace of the one who has knowledge.

208
00:17:41,978 --> 00:17:43,849
He said; this is by the grace of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

209
00:17:43,915 --> 00:17:49,515
That's why it's very important for us always, to believe and to say; whatever good I have done, is from Allah.

210
00:17:50,709 --> 00:17:53,587
And whatever mistakes I have done; are from myself.

211
00:17:54,434 --> 00:17:58,414
Whatever good we do, or happens to us, or anybody does; is from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

212
00:17:58,474 --> 00:18:00,176
And then, Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) said;

213
00:18:00,709 --> 00:18:04,196
لِيَبْلُوَنِي أَأَشْكُرُ أَمْ أَكْفُرُ ۖ

214
00:18:04,616 --> 00:18:10,465
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is testing me to see; whether I am grateful or ungrateful.

215
00:18:11,599 --> 00:18:14,431
Whatever Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given you; and we talked about this a lot.

216
00:18:14,671 --> 00:18:19,417
Whatever Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given you; is a test from Allah for you to see; if you will be grateful or not.

217
00:18:20,651 --> 00:18:21,342
And then, he said;

218
00:18:21,522 --> 00:18:24,142
وَمَن شَكَرَ فَإِنَّمَا يَشْكُرُ لِنَفْسِهِ ۖ

219
00:18:24,649 --> 00:18:28,564
And whoever is grateful, truly his gratitude is for who?

220
00:18:28,904 --> 00:18:29,764
For his own self.

221
00:18:30,051 --> 00:18:35,353
You're not going to benefit Allahسُبحانه وتعالى at all, by being grateful to him; you're benefiting yourself.

222
00:18:35,579 --> 00:18:42,628
وَمَن كَفَرَ فَإِنَّ رَبِّي غَنِيٌّ كَرِيمٌ۝

223
00:18:43,181 --> 00:18:49,084
Whoever is ungrateful; certainly my lord is rich; free of all needs and bountiful.

224
00:18:49,811 --> 00:18:54,271
If you are not grateful; believe me; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى does not need you.

225
00:18:55,738 --> 00:19:03,363
We need to tell ourselves this; because sometimes we feel that the money we pay; we're doing a favour to the religion of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

226
00:19:04,003 --> 00:19:09,878
Whatever we donate of our time, or effort to the religion of Allah, sometimes we brag about it.

227
00:19:10,072 --> 00:19:14,518
The religion of Allah does not need me; it does not need you; it does not need anyone.

228
00:19:15,064 --> 00:19:17,118
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is sufficient of all means.

229
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:20,093
We are doing this for our own benefit.

230
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:24,245
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام said;

231
00:19:24,332 --> 00:19:25,639
قَالَ نَكِّرُواْ لَهَا عَرْشَهَا

232
00:19:26,305 --> 00:19:33,291
He said; Disguise her throne for her; change the outlook of the throne a little bit.

233
00:19:34,584 --> 00:19:36,278
Make some alterations to it.

234
00:19:36,731 --> 00:19:37,384
Why?

235
00:19:37,651 --> 00:19:48,490
قَالَ نَكِّرُواْ لَهَا عَرْشَهَا نَنظُرْ أَتَهْتَدِىٓ أَمْ تَكُونُ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَهْتَدُونَ۝

236
00:19:48,863 --> 00:19:55,832
To see; will she be one of those, who recognize it, or she would be one of those, who won't?

237
00:19:56,646 --> 00:20:01,038
So they made some alterations to her throne; change the way it looks; a little bit.

238
00:20:01,411 --> 00:20:03,111
But the essence of it, was the same.

239
00:20:04,105 --> 00:20:07,684
The uniqueness and the greatness of that throne was untouched.

240
00:20:08,257 --> 00:20:15,510
فَلَمَّا جَآءَتْ قِيلَ أَهَٰكَذَا عَرْشُكِ ۖ

241
00:20:15,930 --> 00:20:20,440
So when she came; it was said to her; Is your throne like this?

242
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:22,480
This is a straightforward question.

243
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:24,213
Yes or no; question.

244
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:25,867
Is this your throne?

245
00:20:26,173 --> 00:20:27,296
What should the answer be?

246
00:20:27,770 --> 00:20:29,000
Yes or no.

247
00:20:30,116 --> 00:20:31,355
Now she said; Yes!

248
00:20:32,515 --> 00:20:34,489
It looks like our throne, but it's a little bit different.

249
00:20:35,095 --> 00:20:36,705
And if she said; No!

250
00:20:37,375 --> 00:20:42,627
It's true that there is some alterations to it, but it's very, very similar to my throne.

251
00:20:44,194 --> 00:20:46,807
So, she avoided the yes or no answer, and she said;

252
00:20:47,173 --> 00:20:48,733
قَالَتْ كَأَنَّهُۥ هُوَ ۚ

253
00:20:48,873 --> 00:20:50,516
A very diplomatic answer.

254
00:20:50,569 --> 00:20:51,422
She said;

255
00:20:52,609 --> 00:20:55,599
It is as though, it were the very same.

256
00:20:56,186 --> 00:20:59,244
So, it's not a yes answer, and it's not a no answer.

257
00:20:59,271 --> 00:21:02,258
And this is part of her wisdom and Hikmah(حكمة).

258
00:21:02,564 --> 00:21:06,520
She didn't give a straight answer of yes or no, and she made her answer right in between.

259
00:21:06,547 --> 00:21:09,640
Because; it looks like her throne but it's a little bit different.

260
00:21:11,007 --> 00:21:12,379
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

261
00:21:12,526 --> 00:21:15,212
وَأُوتِينَا ٱلْعِلْمَ مِن قَبْلِهَا وَكُنَّا مُسْلِمِينَ۝

262
00:21:15,292 --> 00:21:21,749
Sulaimanعليه السلام said; Knowledge was bestowed on us before her, and we were submitting to Allah.

263
00:21:22,102 --> 00:21:33,505
وَصَدَّهَا مَا كَانَت تَّعْبُدُ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ ۖ إِنَّهَا كَانَتْ مِن قَوْمٍۢ كَٰفِرِينَ۝

264
00:21:33,825 --> 00:21:41,191
And that what she used to worship besides Allah, has prevented her from Islam, for she was of a disbelieving people.

265
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:46,246
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is saying; What prevented her from being a Muslim is, because the way; she was brought up.

266
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:51,372
Refusing the gift was one step for her towards Islam.

267
00:21:52,325 --> 00:21:56,439
Bringing the throne was a second step for her, towards Islam.

268
00:21:57,152 --> 00:21:59,852
قِيلَ لَهَا ٱدْخُلِى ٱلصَّرْحَ ۖ

269
00:22:00,385 --> 00:22:02,971
It was said to her, Enter As-Sarkh(اَلصَّرْح).

270
00:22:03,184 --> 00:22:04,178
What is As-Sarkh(اَلصَّرْح).?

271
00:22:04,624 --> 00:22:10,540
As-Sarkh(اَلصَّرْح) is a special palace that was built for Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

272
00:22:12,406 --> 00:22:16,799
This palace had very amazing things in it.

273
00:22:17,272 --> 00:22:21,348
One of which was the flooring of this palace.

274
00:22:22,654 --> 00:22:32,894
The floor was made out of glass; transparent glass, and under that glass was a flowing river.

275
00:22:34,321 --> 00:22:41,004
So this palace is erected on water, and the floor was glass.

276
00:22:41,710 --> 00:22:46,544
Glass was something that the people in that time might not have known; this transparent material.

277
00:22:47,490 --> 00:22:51,890
So when, Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام told her to enter into this palace.

278
00:22:51,937 --> 00:22:53,784
When she saw it; what did she think?

279
00:22:54,877 --> 00:22:58,990
She thought it was water; so she raised up her skirt.

280
00:23:00,316 --> 00:23:01,823
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

281
00:23:02,076 --> 00:23:04,315
قِيلَ لَهَا ٱدْخُلِى ٱلصَّرْحَ ۖ

282
00:23:04,816 --> 00:23:13,256
فَلَمَّا رَأَتْهُ حَسِبَتْهُ لُجَّةً وَكَشَفَتْ عَن سَاقَيْهَا ۚ

283
00:23:14,171 --> 00:23:21,883
But when she saw it; she thought it was a pool, and she tucked up her clothes uncovering her legs.

284
00:23:23,623 --> 00:23:25,029
Something very embarrassing.

285
00:23:26,102 --> 00:23:27,112
Why is it embarrassing?

286
00:23:27,152 --> 00:23:28,693
Because, it shows her ignorance.

287
00:23:28,993 --> 00:23:33,691
It shows that, she's backward considering the advanced age that Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان) was at.

288
00:23:33,784 --> 00:23:35,564
She doesn't know about this technology.

289
00:23:35,857 --> 00:23:39,863
She was raising up her skirt, trying to walk into that water.

290
00:23:39,943 --> 00:23:41,430
So it was embarrassing for her.

291
00:23:42,090 --> 00:23:44,163
Why did Sulaiman(سليمان) do all of this?

292
00:23:44,677 --> 00:23:48,199
Again to show her, what Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given him?

293
00:23:48,972 --> 00:23:56,758
It's part of the miracle of what Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given him, to show to her, the truth of His message.

294
00:23:57,251 --> 00:23:59,561
Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام told her;

295
00:23:59,938 --> 00:24:06,970
قَالَ إِنَّهُۥ صَرْحٌ مُّمَرَّدٌ مِّن قَوَارِيرَ ۗ

296
00:24:07,290 --> 00:24:11,475
He said; Verily it is a glass surface with water underneath it.

297
00:24:11,875 --> 00:24:17,332
In that moment, that was the third step towards Islam for her.

298
00:24:17,785 --> 00:24:21,452
Finally, finally Bilqees(بلقيس) submitted and said;

299
00:24:21,785 --> 00:24:32,231
قَالَتْ رَبِّ إِنِّى ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِى وَأَسْلَمْتُ مَعَ سُلَيْمَٰنَ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ۝

300
00:24:32,631 --> 00:24:33,998
She said; My Lord!

301
00:24:34,244 --> 00:24:43,301
Verily, I have wronged myself, and I submit to Allah; the Lord of Al-Alameen(اَلْعَٰلَمِينَ); the Lord of the world and she became a Muslim.

302
00:24:45,196 --> 00:24:48,325
That's the end of the story in Qur'an.

303
00:24:48,498 --> 00:24:50,152
And again, we don't go beyond that.

304
00:24:50,192 --> 00:24:53,820
Because, there's many fairy tales about; what happened after that.

305
00:24:54,713 --> 00:24:58,753
And there is no proof of the authenticity of any of these stories.

306
00:24:58,847 --> 00:25:04,632
They say that Sulaimanعليه السلام married Bilqees(بلقيس) and it is turned into a romantic story.

307
00:25:05,145 --> 00:25:14,834
And we do not again, get in this, because if it's not true, it is being very disrespectful with the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

308
00:25:14,854 --> 00:25:16,128
So we avoid it completely.

309
00:25:16,521 --> 00:25:22,290
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى again; whatever has been mentioned in Qur'an is for us to learn the lessons from, Al-Ibrah(العبرة).

310
00:25:22,523 --> 00:25:27,083
And whatever has not been mentioned in Qur'an; has not been mentioned because, there's no Ibrah(عبرة) in it, there's no lesson in it.

311
00:25:27,570 --> 00:25:34,212
And we need to be practical and learn what will benefit us, Al-Ilm an-Nafia(اَلْعِلْمَ النّافِعَ); the beneficial knowledge.

312
00:25:34,592 --> 00:25:40,706
And get away from the knowledge; that doesn't do us any good, and doesn't have any practicality or applications for it.

313
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:49,925
Essence of the story is that; at the end, Bilqees(بلقيس) became a Muslim, after she saw; what Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Sulaimanعليه السلام.

314
00:25:50,065 --> 00:25:56,404
We move on to another part of the story of Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

315
00:25:56,784 --> 00:26:06,946
In the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ and until now, a lot of things have been attributed to Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام, which are untrue.

316
00:26:07,973 --> 00:26:09,440
One of which, is magic.

317
00:26:11,346 --> 00:26:17,888
There are some of Al-Yahood(اليهود); the Jews, who attribute magic to Sayidina Sulaiman(سيدنا سليمان),

318
00:26:19,008 --> 00:26:24,817
and the whole story of the temple also, is attributed to Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

319
00:26:25,530 --> 00:26:29,344
For example, the Jews, or the people of the book.

320
00:26:30,197 --> 00:26:37,829
They associate Sulaimanعليه السلام with someone called; Asmodeus.

321
00:26:38,163 --> 00:26:41,129
A S M O D E U S

322
00:26:41,525 --> 00:26:45,065
And this Asmodeus was the chief of the devils.

323
00:26:46,225 --> 00:26:49,611
And they associate him with Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام,

324
00:26:49,824 --> 00:26:59,659
and they say that this devil; chief of the devils was the one who assisted Sulaiman(سليمان) in building and constructing.

325
00:26:59,972 --> 00:27:05,168
And he is the one, who used to tutor and teach Sulaiman(سليمان) magic.

326
00:27:06,714 --> 00:27:10,076
And to teach him many of the skills that they say, Sulaiman(سليمان) had.

327
00:27:10,543 --> 00:27:17,599
And you would find that many quotes and movements; they attach themselves to Sulaiman(سليمان).

328
00:27:17,879 --> 00:27:22,719
Many of these secret orders; they claim that they go back to Sulaiman(سليمان).

329
00:27:23,745 --> 00:27:28,498
And the most famous of them, is the Masonic movement; Al-Masoniyyah(الماسونيه); the Freemasons.

330
00:27:29,758 --> 00:27:34,004
You would find that the concept of the temple; the Temple of Solomon,

331
00:27:34,398 --> 00:27:41,570
is something that is central or it is very influential, and the ideology of the Freemasons.

332
00:27:41,930 --> 00:27:47,233
Also movements like the Kabalah(كباله) and some of these other, a mystical Jewish cults;

333
00:27:47,553 --> 00:27:54,681
they practice magic which they claim, they have learned from Sulaiman(سليمان) and they claim that the lineage goes back to Sulaiman(سليمان).

334
00:27:54,948 --> 00:28:05,669
Now there is some truth that, there is magic, that goes back in lineage to some very early Jews; but it does not go back to Sayidina Sulaimanعليه السلام.

335
00:28:06,482 --> 00:28:08,202
It all goes back to where?

336
00:28:08,862 --> 00:28:14,978
Where did the Jews learned this magic, that some of which still exists until now?

337
00:28:14,998 --> 00:28:17,861
